112-
113-The metal set is the ten metals: Pb, Cd, iAs, tAs, tHg, Ni, Al, Cr, Sn, U. See [[docs/schema-history]] for migration history. Cr carries total chromium; Cr-VI lives on `metals/chromium-hexavalent`. MeHg is matrix-driven and not in the ingredient profile.
114-
115-### Mandatory ingredient-page sections (enforced)
116-
117-Every non-stub ingredient page must carry these `## H2` headings in order. Stubs (all-pending `contamination_profile`, no contributing sources) are exempt. The lint check in CLAUDE.md Part 18 enforces these; failed pages surface via the `COMPLETE-INGREDIENT-SECTIONS` action.
118-
119-1. `## Why this commodity accumulates heavy metals` — soil, plant biology, processing, or sourcing reason. One to three paragraphs of prose.
120-2. `## Heavy metal contamination profile` — body-level synthesis table (see Body table section below). Generator-managed; never hand-edited inside its marker bounds.
121-3. `## Ranges by source, region, and variety` — geographic and varietal variation, anchored on sources.
122-4. `## Processing effects` — polishing, rinsing, parboiling, fermentation, drying, milling, refining. Cite the source for each claim.
123-5. `## Ingredient-derivative risk` — derivatives that concentrate or dilute which metals. Bran-vs-whole-vs-white is the canonical case.
124-6. `## Mitigation options` — practical interventions ordered by impact magnitude. Subsection order: sourcing → agronomic → processing → formulation → testing/QC → packaging/storage. Each lever is a one-paragraph entry naming the magnitude with a cited source. Cross-link to dedicated `mitigation/<topic>.md` pages.
125-7. `## Regulatory limits that apply` — Codex, EU, FDA, and other operative limits. Limit value, matrix scope, basis (product as placed, as consumed, dry weight). Cross-link to `regulations/<rule-id>`.
126-8. `## Sources` — source legend table auto-generated by `tools/evidence/build-source-legend.mjs`.
127-
128-Stub pages carry only sections 2 (body table, all rows marked data gap) and 8 (source legend with empty-corpus message). When a stub crosses two-plus contributing A-tier sources, the section-completion subprocess action drafts sections 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 from the routing audit and contributing source pages.
129-
130-The `contamination_profile` block is deliberately machine-readable. The app consumes it directly.
131-
132-### Geographic and seasonal variance sub-fields
133-
134-Each metal sub-block carries two optional variance arrays — `geographic_breakdown` and `seasonal_variance` — that hold regional and harvest-period range data brand legal teams need to defend against a cherry-picked-maximum attack. See OPERATING.md Part 7 initiative 7.
